ioprobe -- capture the I/O probes behind XSysInfo's "Clock" and "Gary rev"
lines, with addresses and returned values, so two cores can be compared
directly instead of comparing two summary panels.

  vc +aos68k -O1 -cpu=68040 -o ioprobe ioprobe.c     (vbcc, /opt/amiga-cc)

Run it from a CLI on each core with the same ROM, the same OSD settings and
the same Workbench, and diff the output.  It prints every individual read,
not just the conclusion, because GAYLEID is a sequence: a write resets its
counter and each read shifts out one bit, so a change in the shape of the
read strobes -- not only in the data -- changes the identity a probe
computes.  A summary panel cannot distinguish that from a settings
difference; the per-read values can.
